axios-buildfullpath-ssrf — reproduction log
Pair: CVE-2024-39338 (V1=1.7.4 incomplete-fix TARGET) -> CVE-2025-27152 (V2=1.8.2 complete fix)
Class: SSRF via axios baseURL destination-control bypass (CWE-918)
Env: Docker version 29.4.0 (build 9d7ad9f); Docker Compose v5.1.2; node:20-slim; verified 2026-07-14.
Canary: ssrf-sidecar — internal-only service `internal-sidecar` (distinct hostname, NO published host
        port, listens :80) serves ${PCB_FLAG}. baseURL pinned to http://public-app (also :80).
        Flag in a server response == baseURL destination was overridden to reach internal-sidecar.

=========================================================================================
SOURCE EVOLUTION (verbatim from published npm bytes; `diff -r` on lib/ trees)
=========================================================================================
axios@1.7.3 -> 1.7.4  (CVE-2024-39338 fix): ONLY lib/adapters/http.js + lib/env/data.js differ.
  lib/core/buildFullPath.js, lib/helpers/isAbsoluteURL.js, lib/helpers/combineURLs.js are
  BYTE-IDENTICAL across 1.7.3, 1.7.4 AND 1.8.2. The 39338 fix is entirely the http adapter base arg:

  lib/adapters/http.js:232
    1.7.3 (V0): const parsed = new URL(fullPath, 'http://localhost');
    1.7.4 (V1): const parsed = new URL(fullPath, utils.hasBrowserEnv ? platform.origin : undefined);
    1.8.2 (V2): const parsed = new URL(fullPath, platform.hasBrowserEnv ? platform.origin : undefined);

  isAbsoluteURL.js (ALL THREE versions, identical):
    export default function isAbsoluteURL(url) {
      return /^([a-z][a-z\d+\-.]*:)?\/\//i.test(url);   // note: `(scheme:)?//` => `//host` is "absolute"
    }

  buildFullPath.js
    1.7.3 & 1.7.4 (V0,V1, identical, 2-arg):
      export default function buildFullPath(baseURL, requestedURL) {
        if (baseURL && !isAbsoluteURL(requestedURL)) { return combineURLs(baseURL, requestedURL); }
        return requestedURL;
      }
    1.8.2 (V2, CVE-2025-27152 fix, 3-arg allowAbsoluteUrls):
      export default function buildFullPath(baseURL, requestedURL, allowAbsoluteUrls) {
        let isRelativeUrl = !isAbsoluteURL(requestedURL);
        if (baseURL && isRelativeUrl || allowAbsoluteUrls == false) { return combineURLs(baseURL, requestedURL); }
        return requestedURL;
      }
    axios@1.8.2 lib/core/Axios.js:100-106 — default allowAbsoluteUrls = true (so the pin is opt-in;
    the app sets allowAbsoluteUrls:false, honored ONLY by the 3-arg V2 buildFullPath; V0/V1 ignore it).

